Overview
Explain the problem you solve, target users, and the core idea in 2–3 sentences.

Features
Feature 1: short description (e.g., CRUD for tasks)

Feature 2: short description (e.g., Authentication stub)

Feature 3: short description (e.g., Offline storage on Android)

Feature 4: short description (e.g., Responsive UI, animations)

Tech Stack
Frontend: React, React Router, Redux (or Context), Reactstrap/CSS

Backend: Django (Django REST Framework optional)

Mobile: Android (Kotlin/Java) or Kivy (Python) for simple app

Database: SQLite (Android), PostgreSQL/SQLite (Django)

Tools: Node.js, npm/yarn, Android Studio, Git, json-server (for mock APIs)

Setup and Installation
Clone the repo: git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/<repo-name>.git

Frontend:

cd frontend

npm install

Backend:

cd backend

python -m venv venv

source venv/bin/activate (Linux/Mac) or venv\Scripts\activate (Windows)

pip install -r requirements.txt

python manage.py migrate

Android:

Open android/ in Android Studio

Configure device/emulator and build

Run Locally
Start backend (Django): cd backend source venv/bin/activate python manage.py runserver

Start frontend (React): cd frontend npm start

Android:

Run via Android Studio on emulator/device

API Endpoints (example)
GET /api/items/ — list items

POST /api/items/ — create item

GET /api/items/:id/ — get item

PUT /api/items/:id/ — update item

DELETE /api/items/:id/ — delete item

Folder Structure
/backend — Django project and apps

/frontend — React app (src, public)

/android — Android Studio project (app)

/docs or /assets — screenshots, UML diagrams, reports

/labs — lab scripts, SQL dumps, SSIS/SSAS notes (if any)

README.md, LICENSE, requirements.txt, package.json

Usage
Quick demo steps:

Start backend and frontend.

Open http://localhost:3000 (React) and test CRUD operations.

Optionally run Android app to sync with backend or use mock API.

Tests
Frontend:

npm test (React tests)

Backend:

python manage.py test

Android:

Use Android Studio test runner for unit/instrumentation tests

Lab Deliverables
List of required lab items (tick before submission):

[ ] React: SPA with Router, Hooks, Redux, form validation

[ ] Django: CRUD API + sample data

[ ] Android: Multi-activity app with SQLite and one hardware feature

[ ] Java Lab: socket & JDBC demos

[ ] BI Lab: CSV → DB ETL demo, sample report screenshots

Project Report & Presentation
Short report: 1–2 pages including objective, design choices, architecture diagram, challenges, future work.

Slides: 5–8 slides (Title, Problem, Architecture, Demo screenshots, Conclusion).

Put both in /docs as report.pdf and slides.pdf..

Contributing
Fork the repo, create a feature branch (feature/xyz), implement, push, and open a Pull Request with description and testing notes.

Keep commits small and atomic. Use clear commit messages.
